WEBVTT

00:00:01.620 --> 00:00:03.450
Now it's begun!

00:00:03.450 --> 00:00:06.200
The WBA World Featherweight Title Match!

00:00:06.200 --> 00:00:11.070
Who will have his name engraved in history as the strongest featherweight?

00:00:14.560 --> 00:00:16.020
A left!

00:00:20.550 --> 00:00:22.520
Another left!

00:00:22.520 --> 00:00:25.530
It lands as the champion's hand was knocked aside!

00:00:36.780 --> 00:00:40.130
The opening hit is a left from the challenger!

00:00:40.560 --> 00:00:42.880
H-He hit him!

00:00:42.880 --> 00:00:46.380
But I couldn't hit him no matter what kind of feint I used.

00:00:46.380 --> 00:00:49.020
Cheap feints won't make a difference against that guy.

00:00:50.130 --> 00:00:52.140
The old man intended to hit him right from the start.

00:00:52.340 --> 00:00:54.620
So he busted his guard open with that first left...

00:00:54.620 --> 00:00:56.440
...and then slammed one home while he was open!

00:00:56.440 --> 00:01:02.370
On the world stage, sometimes being aggressive is more useful than fancy tactics.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:03.710
That's Date-san for you.

00:01:03.710 --> 00:01:07.230
Well, now the champion's gonna get serious too!

00:01:07.230 --> 00:01:09.410
The old man sure started things off with a bang!

00:01:12.500 --> 00:01:13.890
Date moves in!

00:01:13.890 --> 00:01:16.070
He's not letting the champion get into his rhythm!

00:01:16.070 --> 00:01:17.060
<i>Sorry,</i>

00:01:17.060 --> 00:01:19.690
<i>but there's no way in hell I'm letting you get into your rhythm.</i>

00:01:19.690 --> 00:01:22.290
<i>Once that happens, you dominate a lopsided match!</i>

00:01:22.290 --> 00:01:24.620
<i>I learned that the hard way seven years ago!</i>

00:01:24.970 --> 00:01:26.620
The challenger is throwing combos!

00:01:26.620 --> 00:01:28.390
He's pushed the champion to the ropes already!

00:01:29.110 --> 00:01:31.850
He's using a fighter-type approach similar to Ippo's style.

00:01:31.850 --> 00:01:33.400
Don't get the wrong idea.

00:01:33.400 --> 00:01:37.690
Keeping a solid form and countering things calmly is his post-retirement style.

00:01:37.690 --> 00:01:39.490
So that's...

00:01:39.490 --> 00:01:41.230
Suppressive boxing!

00:01:42.140 --> 00:01:44.280
That's the style he used before he retired!

00:01:45.010 --> 00:01:47.660
<i>I feel like I've been caught in a time warp.</i>

00:01:47.960 --> 00:01:50.230
<i>But it's fitting for this world title match.</i>

00:01:50.230 --> 00:01:52.000
<i>You've set the pace! Go for it!</i>

00:01:52.320 --> 00:01:55.330
The champion's showing his experience too.

00:01:55.330 --> 00:01:59.740
A rush like that would be enough to push someone back, but...

00:01:59.740 --> 00:02:00.600
You're right.

00:02:00.600 --> 00:02:01.550
He's watching closely...

00:02:02.260 --> 00:02:04.650
His expression is incredibly calm.

00:02:04.650 --> 00:02:07.290
The champion's keeping his cool.

00:02:07.290 --> 00:02:09.300
And if Date-san maintains that attack against someone who's keeping his cool, then...

00:02:10.510 --> 00:02:11.600
Whoa!

00:02:11.600 --> 00:02:13.620
And the champion switches their positions!

00:02:13.620 --> 00:02:15.950
A reversal at the ropes!

00:02:15.950 --> 00:02:17.310
I-Incredible!

00:02:17.310 --> 00:02:18.210
That's what I was worried about!

00:02:18.210 --> 00:02:20.290
Shit! He's gonna get nailed now!

00:02:23.080 --> 00:02:25.110
A left from the champion!

00:02:26.800 --> 00:02:28.610
<i>That left extends farther than that!</i>

00:02:28.610 --> 00:02:30.120
<i>It can't be dodged with a sway!</i>

00:02:33.940 --> 00:02:37.130
The challenger escapes from the ropes without taking any damage!

00:02:37.130 --> 00:02:39.380
It's a breathtaking high-level exchange!

00:02:40.030 --> 00:02:43.030
I took so many of those extending lefts...

00:02:43.030 --> 00:02:46.060
That's the same neck-twisting he used in his match against you.

00:02:46.060 --> 00:02:49.760
Actually, the old man's body probably remembers the champion's punches,

00:02:50.370 --> 00:02:52.720
and that neck twist was probably something he cooked up for this.

00:02:52.720 --> 00:02:54.640
In fact, every match he's had since then...

00:02:54.640 --> 00:02:57.810
may have been practice for this world title match!

00:02:59.110 --> 00:03:01.770
And now the fighters face off in the center of the ring again.

00:03:03.110 --> 00:03:05.170
The champion takes the offensive this time!

00:03:05.170 --> 00:03:06.440
The challenger returns fire!

00:03:06.440 --> 00:03:07.960
Neither is connecting!

00:03:07.960 --> 00:03:09.360
It's an exchange of lefts!

00:03:09.360 --> 00:03:12.270
Their lefts are about even.

00:03:12.270 --> 00:03:14.310
It's what I'd expect from Date-san, but still...

00:03:14.310 --> 00:03:16.110
This is amazing...

00:03:16.110 --> 00:03:19.000
Being able to stand on even footing with the world champion...

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:20.650
Come to think of it...

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:24.440
the champion never used his right in his spar with me.

00:03:24.440 --> 00:03:28.550
If their lefts are even, then their rights may be the key to this.

00:03:29.110 --> 00:03:30.790
But when will they use them,

00:03:30.790 --> 00:03:32.510
and who will go first?

00:03:33.380 --> 00:03:35.540
Both fighters connect with their lefts!

00:03:35.540 --> 00:03:37.230
Their faces are knocked upward slightly!

00:03:37.230 --> 00:03:38.530
So sharp!

00:03:38.530 --> 00:03:40.190
Was it a dual exchange!?

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:46.610
A right!

00:03:48.030 --> 00:03:50.260
Whoa, and there's the bell!

00:03:50.260 --> 00:03:52.350
The first round is complete!

00:03:52.350 --> 00:03:55.140
You can feel the entire arena trying to catch its breath!

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:57.660
There's finally a break in the tension.

00:03:57.660 --> 00:03:59.950
That's how intense these past three minutes were!

00:03:59.950 --> 00:04:02.170
What's gonna happen in this match?

00:04:02.750 --> 00:04:05.020
If this goes for all 12 rounds, I'm not gonna make it.

00:04:05.020 --> 00:04:07.050
It's way too tense.

00:04:07.050 --> 00:04:10.390
Since that first left landed cleanly...

00:04:10.850 --> 00:04:12.950
the old man won the first round 10-9!

00:04:12.950 --> 00:04:14.700
He took the point lead!

00:04:14.700 --> 00:04:16.660
Hopefully he'll take the next round too.

00:04:16.660 --> 00:04:18.830
I can't make any specific predictions,

00:04:18.830 --> 00:04:21.650
but I get the feeling the next round's gonna be rough.

00:04:22.100 --> 00:04:25.670
They were both ready to use their rights,

00:04:25.670 --> 00:04:28.440
which means they were ready to fire their big guns.

00:04:28.440 --> 00:04:31.320
They both seem to have each other's timing down.

00:04:31.320 --> 00:04:34.450
It may be harder to make a move, but...

00:04:34.680 --> 00:04:35.610
Yeah...

00:04:35.610 --> 00:04:38.700
once he gets his chance, the match could end in an instant!

00:04:39.510 --> 00:04:40.490
An instant...

00:04:41.530 --> 00:04:44.390
Looks like he got your greeting.

00:04:44.390 --> 00:04:46.850
"Long time, no see." That sounds about right.

00:04:46.850 --> 00:04:49.460
So, how was the champion?

00:04:49.740 --> 00:04:51.530
I can't tell.

00:04:51.530 --> 00:04:54.590
He's definitely still holding back.

00:04:54.590 --> 00:04:56.020
Don't get anxious!

00:04:56.020 --> 00:04:58.140
You've taken the pace!

00:04:58.780 --> 00:05:00.600
You sure...

00:05:00.930 --> 00:05:03.310
that you're not the one who's getting anxious, Pops?

00:05:04.330 --> 00:05:05.150
Eiji...

00:05:05.150 --> 00:05:05.860
I don't blame you.

00:05:06.460 --> 00:05:08.750
Last time, I lost in the second round.

00:05:08.750 --> 00:05:10.760
In other words, in this next round.

00:05:10.760 --> 00:05:12.990
It's no wonder you'd be worried.

00:05:13.410 --> 00:05:16.990
But it's time to cast off those worries!

00:05:16.990 --> 00:05:19.470
I'm not the same as I was seven years ago!

00:05:21.280 --> 00:05:23.340
He's pretty tough.

00:05:23.340 --> 00:05:25.880
He's leveled up significantly since last time.

00:05:26.470 --> 00:05:28.060
It's not a problem.

00:05:28.060 --> 00:05:30.380
I've leveled up as well,

00:05:31.010 --> 00:05:33.960
so the difference between us hasn't changed.

00:05:33.960 --> 00:05:34.780
Which means...

00:05:36.190 --> 00:05:38.170
it ends...

00:05:38.680 --> 00:05:40.270
in the next round.

00:05:41.430 --> 00:05:42.780
Seconds out!

00:05:42.780 --> 00:05:44.470
And now, the second round!

00:05:44.470 --> 00:05:47.290
Things are bound to be even more tense than they were in the first round!

00:05:47.290 --> 00:05:50.350
How are things going to shape up!?

00:05:53.920 --> 00:05:54.530
What the hell?

00:05:54.960 --> 00:05:57.610
How come it got quiet all of a sudden?

00:05:57.610 --> 00:06:00.410
I can understand why they'd want to watch in silence.

00:06:00.410 --> 00:06:06.000
The entire arena knows that this was the round the old man lost in last time.

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:09.540
If things are the same as they were seven years ago, then the old man will lose in this round.

00:06:10.490 --> 00:06:11.920
If he survives,

00:06:12.120 --> 00:06:15.350
that means he's gotten that much closer to the world title.

00:06:17.400 --> 00:06:18.430
<i>Eiji...</i>

00:06:18.430 --> 00:06:22.680
<i>I'm sure you're the one who feels most anxious about this.</i>

00:06:22.680 --> 00:06:25.450
<i>That's why you came out and said it, right?</i>

00:06:25.450 --> 00:06:31.190
<i>I'm sure your head is echoing the despair and humiliation of what you went through in Mexico,</i>

00:06:31.420 --> 00:06:34.530
<i>but you have to cut yourself free and move past that tragedy.</i>

00:06:35.490 --> 00:06:36.670
The challenger makes his move!

00:06:36.670 --> 00:06:37.830
A razor sharp left!

00:06:37.830 --> 00:06:39.980
<i>That's right! You have to take the initiative!</i>

00:06:41.430 --> 00:06:43.080
<i>A right all of a sudden?</i>

00:06:43.080 --> 00:06:44.160
<i>But the swing is too large.</i>

00:06:44.160 --> 00:06:46.710
<i>No way I'm taking that punch!</i>

00:07:07.990 --> 00:07:10.660
A sudden right from the champion!

00:07:10.660 --> 00:07:14.440
It missed the mark, but the power alone was enough to give you the chills!

00:07:14.440 --> 00:07:15.540
Wh—

00:07:16.270 --> 00:07:17.750
What a right.

00:07:17.750 --> 00:07:21.150
It's a punch that penetrates past the point it was aiming for!

00:07:21.150 --> 00:07:23.140
If he gets hit with that...

00:07:23.930 --> 00:07:26.450
I'm starting to get goose bumps.

00:07:28.070 --> 00:07:30.460
The champion closes in using shoulder feints!

00:07:30.830 --> 00:07:32.120
Date-san is being pushed back...

00:07:32.120 --> 00:07:33.640
That's not ordinary pressure.

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:35.210
This is the world's greatest pressure we're talking about!

00:07:35.210 --> 00:07:36.810
The challenger retreats!

00:07:36.810 --> 00:07:39.180
These bluffs are enough to push him to the ropes!

00:07:41.610 --> 00:07:43.220
<i>His body remembers what happened last time,</i>

00:07:43.680 --> 00:07:46.180
<i>and it's hesitating.</i>

00:07:48.180 --> 00:07:49.330
Don't let him intimidate you, Eiji!

00:07:49.330 --> 00:07:50.900
There's nowhere to run!

00:07:50.900 --> 00:07:51.860
You have to face him!

00:07:52.770 --> 00:07:54.450
The challenger takes the initiative!

00:07:54.450 --> 00:07:56.070
But the champion reacts before him!

00:07:56.970 --> 00:07:58.210
A left!

00:07:58.210 --> 00:08:00.280
Did it connect!?

00:08:00.570 --> 00:08:03.280
No, he rolls with it by twisting his neck!

00:08:03.280 --> 00:08:04.610
And sidesteps!

00:08:04.610 --> 00:08:06.290
The challenger's really showing his stuff!

00:08:06.920 --> 00:08:07.800
Amazing!

00:08:07.800 --> 00:08:11.120
With his neck-twisting and that sidestep, he'll be fine even if he's against the ropes!

00:08:14.090 --> 00:08:15.670
But what's this!?

00:08:15.670 --> 00:08:17.120
The champion has anticipated his escape route!

00:08:17.120 --> 00:08:19.630
With his path cut off, he's trapped in the corner!

00:08:19.940 --> 00:08:22.430
<i>Looks like he's predicting my moves!</i>

00:08:23.060 --> 00:08:25.530
The champion switches his aim from the head to the body!

00:08:25.530 --> 00:08:27.430
It's a focused attack to the midsection with lefts!

00:08:28.180 --> 00:08:29.220
Crap, he can't stay in the corner!

00:08:29.220 --> 00:08:30.810
Run, Date-san!

00:08:30.810 --> 00:08:32.680
He can't.

00:08:32.680 --> 00:08:34.690
Ricardo's throwing enough body blows to push him back.

00:08:34.690 --> 00:08:38.060
He can't use his neck-twisting trick if his body is what's being hit.

00:08:38.060 --> 00:08:39.440
There's no way to escape!

00:08:39.440 --> 00:08:41.490
<i>This is a world title match.</i>

00:08:41.490 --> 00:08:45.410
<i>The same trick's not going to work twice.</i>

00:08:46.350 --> 00:08:48.260
<i>These body blows are bait to get me to attack him.</i>

00:08:48.260 --> 00:08:50.710
<i>The fact that these punches are so light is proof of that.</i>

00:08:51.070 --> 00:08:55.210
<i>He wants me to lower my guard so that he can nail me in the head!</i>

00:08:55.460 --> 00:08:56.710
<i>In that case...</i>

00:08:58.320 --> 00:09:00.720
The challenger lowers his guard without hesitating!

00:09:01.030 --> 00:09:02.120
<i>Bingo!</i>

00:09:02.120 --> 00:09:04.470
<i>You're not the only one who can read strategies!</i>

00:09:04.930 --> 00:09:06.470
He saw it coming!

00:09:06.470 --> 00:09:08.220
The challenger prepares a counter!

00:09:14.970 --> 00:09:17.820
But what gets driven home is a body blow from the champion!

00:09:18.190 --> 00:09:20.820
The challenger ended up taking a counter instead!

00:09:21.190 --> 00:09:24.350
He starts to topple forward!

00:09:31.270 --> 00:09:33.870
The challenger ended up taking a counter instead!

00:09:34.270 --> 00:09:37.410
He starts to topple forward!

00:09:38.530 --> 00:09:42.000
<i>There's no shame in falling from my body blows.</i>

00:09:42.000 --> 00:09:47.520
<i>They've penetrated the heavy armor of countless challengers.</i>

00:09:51.590 --> 00:09:53.170
A one-two from the challenger!

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:55.600
It cleanly connects with the champion's head!

00:09:55.860 --> 00:09:58.460
<i>The angle and timing were perfect.</i>

00:09:58.460 --> 00:10:00.360
<i>Why wasn't it a critical hit?</i>

00:10:01.430 --> 00:10:03.550
It's turned into an exchange in the corner!

00:10:03.550 --> 00:10:05.310
The champion's landing clean hits!

00:10:05.310 --> 00:10:08.010
The challenger fights back desperately!

00:10:09.350 --> 00:10:10.540
An uppercut!

00:10:10.540 --> 00:10:12.130
His jaw is sent skyward!

00:10:16.370 --> 00:10:18.650
The arrow flies true and finds its target!

00:10:18.650 --> 00:10:22.380
This kind of attack could deform someone's skull!

00:10:22.740 --> 00:10:24.760
<i>There was a lot of feedback.</i>

00:10:28.160 --> 00:10:30.510
<i>He can withstand that?</i>

00:10:30.910 --> 00:10:33.000
<i>That was one hell of a shot.</i>

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:34.640
<i>But if that's all...</i>

00:10:34.640 --> 00:10:35.990
He returns fire!

00:10:35.990 --> 00:10:37.780
The challenger is showing his grit with this counter attack!

00:10:37.780 --> 00:10:39.520
It's an explosive exchange!

00:10:40.170 --> 00:10:41.590
<i>It's hard to believe,</i>

00:10:41.590 --> 00:10:43.200
<i>but in the seven years since we last met,</i>

00:10:43.200 --> 00:10:48.030
<i>you've withstood punches that are equal to or greater than my own.</i>

00:10:48.030 --> 00:10:51.170
<i>I have a hard time believing there's a boxer like that in this country,</i>

00:10:51.720 --> 00:10:54.040
<i>but it's the only possible explanation.</i>

00:11:00.290 --> 00:11:02.540
The referee breaks them up!

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:04.510
The second round is over!

00:11:04.510 --> 00:11:06.680
The challenger survives a tight spot!

00:11:06.680 --> 00:11:09.300
It looks like there won't be a replay of the nightmare from seven years ago!

00:11:09.300 --> 00:11:11.090
How'd you like that?

00:11:11.090 --> 00:11:12.600
I made it!

00:11:12.600 --> 00:11:14.680
Things are different from seven years ago.

00:11:18.250 --> 00:11:19.940
Did you see that, Pops?

00:11:20.240 --> 00:11:21.890
Yeah! You bet I did!

00:11:21.890 --> 00:11:24.430
I've surpassed who I was seven years ago,

00:11:24.430 --> 00:11:28.030
and proved that, at the age of 30, I'm stronger than I ever was!

00:11:28.030 --> 00:11:28.700
Yeah!

00:11:28.700 --> 00:11:31.830
Now, all that's left is to surpass the world champion!

00:11:32.560 --> 00:11:36.440
That right was my best shot...

00:11:36.440 --> 00:11:39.140
yet he was able to take it and fight back.

00:11:40.100 --> 00:11:42.240
I have to admit, I was surprised.

00:11:42.240 --> 00:11:44.620
He must've had the experience...

00:11:44.620 --> 00:11:47.840
That is, the experience of fighting

00:11:48.510 --> 00:11:51.910
a powerful puncher comparable to you, and he survived that battle to make it here today.

00:11:52.520 --> 00:11:55.600
I'll admit that I underestimated him.

00:11:56.080 --> 00:11:57.990
I see... he's a fierce opponent.

00:11:58.630 --> 00:12:00.350
Watching him reminds me...

00:12:01.160 --> 00:12:05.030
Maybe it's because I've become too used to this stage called a world title defense.

00:12:05.030 --> 00:12:09.570
Before I knew it, all I was doing was merely repeating my duty to defend the belt.

00:12:09.790 --> 00:12:11.930
I grew tired of it.

00:12:12.460 --> 00:12:16.120
Perhaps it wouldn't be so bad if I returned to how I once was.

00:12:16.980 --> 00:12:17.580
Yes!

00:12:18.140 --> 00:12:20.400
He made it through the second round, Takamura-san!

00:12:20.400 --> 00:12:22.870
That's proof he's gotten closer to the world title!

00:12:22.870 --> 00:12:23.970
Right!

00:12:23.970 --> 00:12:26.830
Even when he was cornered, he was able to fight back!

00:12:26.830 --> 00:12:29.520
If he can fight back even when he's being hit,

00:12:29.520 --> 00:12:31.820
the champ's gonna have a hard time choosing his shots!

00:12:31.820 --> 00:12:33.310
Awesome!

00:12:33.310 --> 00:12:35.560
To be able to withstand those punches and fight back against them!

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:36.950
You're damn right!

00:12:36.950 --> 00:12:39.100
Date-san's our representative, after all!

00:12:39.100 --> 00:12:41.570
It's a straight path to the belt from here on out!

00:12:42.510 --> 00:12:44.560
Seconds out!

00:12:44.560 --> 00:12:48.730
Now, the bell for the third round rings amidst roaring cheers!

00:12:48.730 --> 00:12:49.570
Whoa!

00:12:51.020 --> 00:12:53.100
The champion suddenly goes on the attack!

00:12:53.100 --> 00:12:55.330
The challenger is caught off-guard!

00:12:55.330 --> 00:12:57.630
A right is thrown, as if to silence the cheers!

00:12:57.630 --> 00:12:59.290
Now, a combination!

00:12:59.290 --> 00:13:01.750
The challenger is trapped in the corner!

00:13:01.750 --> 00:13:03.790
The champion's on a rampage!

00:13:03.790 --> 00:13:05.600
Eiji! You have to fight back!

00:13:05.600 --> 00:13:07.250
Don't let him take the lead!

00:13:08.340 --> 00:13:12.050
<i>Even if I wanted to fight back, his timing's completely different!</i>

00:13:12.550 --> 00:13:17.560
<i>All these rough punches make it feel like I'm fighting a totally different person!</i>

00:13:18.060 --> 00:13:20.560
<i>I can't let my guard down!</i>

00:13:20.560 --> 00:13:22.670
T-Takamura-san, what's going on!?

00:13:22.670 --> 00:13:24.940
I thought he was supposed to have trouble choosing his punches, but he's throwing more than before!

00:13:24.940 --> 00:13:25.820
Shut up!

00:13:25.820 --> 00:13:27.320
I'm just as surprised!

00:13:28.400 --> 00:13:32.030
I thought he was some fine-tuned machine, but...

00:13:32.030 --> 00:13:36.300
it's plain to see that these violent punches suit him much better.

00:13:36.300 --> 00:13:37.160
There's no doubt about it!

00:13:38.020 --> 00:13:41.590
This style is Ricardo Martinez showing his true face!

00:13:42.420 --> 00:13:44.960
True face?

00:13:45.250 --> 00:13:47.860
<i>Eiji Date made a huge mistake.</i>

00:13:47.860 --> 00:13:53.800
<i>He forced Ricardo to accept him as a formidable opponent and reminded him of his old style.</i>

00:13:54.340 --> 00:13:57.160
<i>Expert skills aren't enough to take the world title.</i>

00:13:57.160 --> 00:14:00.810
<i>At times, you need the savagery to paint the ring red with blood.</i>

00:14:01.710 --> 00:14:05.540
<i>The perfect fusion of science and violence...</i>

00:14:05.540 --> 00:14:08.900
<i>This is the true Ricardo using his strongest style!</i>

00:14:09.820 --> 00:14:12.100
The champion lays it on thick over the challenger's guard!

00:14:12.100 --> 00:14:13.820
The challenger's caught empty handed!

00:14:14.040 --> 00:14:15.200
<i>Damn it!</i>

00:14:15.200 --> 00:14:17.530
<i>I can practically see him baring his fangs! {Spell check baring bareing bearing}</i>

00:14:17.530 --> 00:14:19.700
<i>But there's no place to run inside the ring!</i>

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:21.430
<i>So I have to bite back!</i>

00:14:22.330 --> 00:14:25.140
That counter made it look like the champion saw it coming from a mile away!

00:14:25.140 --> 00:14:26.170
Did it get him?

00:14:27.040 --> 00:14:30.700
<i>I know that he won't fall from this.</i>

00:14:30.700 --> 00:14:35.930
<i>No matter what hits him, I doubt physical pain would be enough to knock him down today.</i>

00:14:36.620 --> 00:14:41.080
<i>He's come to this match with that kind of absolute determination.</i>

00:14:41.080 --> 00:14:42.430
<i>If I want to beat him,</i>

00:14:42.780 --> 00:14:44.260
<i>I need to attack his spirit, not his body.</i>

00:14:44.260 --> 00:14:46.560
<i>An attack that will sever his consciousness!</i>

00:14:58.240 --> 00:14:59.990
<i>What willpower...</i>

00:14:59.990 --> 00:15:03.060
<i>He's still able to remain conscious after that?</i>

00:15:03.060 --> 00:15:03.910
<i>But...</i>

00:15:04.130 --> 00:15:05.520
He fights back!

00:15:05.520 --> 00:15:07.480
The challenger stubbornly resists!

00:15:07.480 --> 00:15:08.920
But he's having trouble keeping up!

00:15:09.220 --> 00:15:10.740
Damn it!

00:15:10.740 --> 00:15:12.360
He's hanging in there, but...

00:15:12.360 --> 00:15:15.170
...he's just getting beat on mercilessly.

00:15:15.590 --> 00:15:18.080
Does that really look like just a beating?

00:15:18.080 --> 00:15:21.180
It's an exchange of high level defensive and offensive skills.

00:15:21.490 --> 00:15:23.380
I-It sure as hell doesn't look like an exchange!

00:15:23.380 --> 00:15:25.120
It looks completely lopsided!

00:15:25.120 --> 00:15:25.930
I know!

00:15:26.680 --> 00:15:30.440
That's just how big the difference between them is.

00:15:30.440 --> 00:15:34.550
After he survived the second round, I thought he had moved closer to the title.

00:15:34.550 --> 00:15:38.070
And the truth is that the old man has more than enough strength to take on the world.

00:15:38.400 --> 00:15:41.570
But his opponent is <i>out of this world.</i>

00:15:42.460 --> 00:15:44.580
He's on a whole other level.

00:15:45.030 --> 00:15:46.520
It...

00:15:46.520 --> 00:15:47.840
It can't be.

00:15:49.060 --> 00:15:51.390
Dark clouds are surrounding the Ryogoku Kokugikan arena!

00:15:51.390 --> 00:15:54.480
Ever since the third round, the champion has been on a vicious one-sided assault!

00:15:54.480 --> 00:15:57.370
All the challenger can do is endure this brutal development!

00:15:57.370 --> 00:16:00.750
The audience has fallen silent in the face of this legendary strength!

00:16:00.750 --> 00:16:04.170
Is the wall around the world title simply too high to surmount?

00:16:06.810 --> 00:16:07.840
What...

00:16:08.310 --> 00:16:10.140
round is it...

00:16:10.140 --> 00:16:11.100
Pops?

00:16:11.420 --> 00:16:12.830
Don't talk!

00:16:12.830 --> 00:16:15.360
Focus on resting your body!

00:16:15.360 --> 00:16:16.820
This is going to be the ninth round.

00:16:17.620 --> 00:16:20.180
So we're finally in the second half.

00:16:20.180 --> 00:16:22.570
This match is a real pain in the ass.

00:16:24.180 --> 00:16:25.450
A-Are you injured!?

00:16:26.420 --> 00:16:27.470
No big deal...

00:16:28.010 --> 00:16:30.870
just two or three of my ribs.

00:16:31.090 --> 00:16:32.770
Fractures!?

00:16:32.770 --> 00:16:34.420
When did you...

00:16:34.420 --> 00:16:38.650
Look, if you keep being stubborn, things are going to get out of hand!

00:16:38.650 --> 00:16:41.840
And I'll throw this in before I let that happen!

00:16:42.840 --> 00:16:45.460
Give me a break.

00:16:45.460 --> 00:16:49.390
This is where I take the world title.

00:16:51.440 --> 00:16:54.690
Bill, how many of my punches have landed?

00:16:54.690 --> 00:16:57.620
I haven't been counting... but too many to keep track of.

00:16:57.620 --> 00:16:58.880
That's right.

00:16:58.880 --> 00:17:01.530
I've connected that many times.

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:03.410
And yet, he's still standing.

00:17:03.770 --> 00:17:05.910
He's incredibly tough.

00:17:06.400 --> 00:17:10.610
Is his dream of becoming world champion what's keeping him up?

00:17:10.610 --> 00:17:13.370
Or maybe his desire for revenge?

00:17:14.120 --> 00:17:16.760
<i>Dreams... Revenge...</i>

00:17:16.760 --> 00:17:18.430
<i>Those can't be it.</i>

00:17:18.430 --> 00:17:21.790
<i>I've destroyed plenty of challengers who fought with those kind of ambitions.</i>

00:17:21.790 --> 00:17:22.930
<i>But...</i>

00:17:22.930 --> 00:17:25.250
<i>there's no hint of despair in his eyes.</i>

00:17:25.740 --> 00:17:28.510
<i>What's keeping him up?</i>

00:17:29.270 --> 00:17:31.470
I can't watch anymore.

00:17:31.470 --> 00:17:35.770
Having survived this long against the legendary champion is impressive enough.

00:17:35.770 --> 00:17:37.170
What are you talking about!?

00:17:37.170 --> 00:17:38.980
It's not over yet!

00:17:38.980 --> 00:17:42.040
I know how you feel,

00:17:42.040 --> 00:17:43.550
but Date-san is all torn up.

00:17:43.550 --> 00:17:46.710
This guy's got even more experience than Date-san.

00:17:46.710 --> 00:17:48.660
I can't imagine him screwing up.

00:17:48.950 --> 00:17:52.230
There's no way he can turn this around unless he's got some kind of magic trick up his sleeve.

00:17:54.960 --> 00:17:56.030
He does!

00:17:56.030 --> 00:17:57.170
A magic punch!

00:17:58.020 --> 00:17:59.360
I get it.

00:17:59.360 --> 00:18:03.050
The old man hasn't thrown a single punch below the chest the entire match.

00:18:03.050 --> 00:18:06.040
It was probably to keep the champion focused on protecting his head.

00:18:06.040 --> 00:18:07.780
Chest?

00:18:15.090 --> 00:18:19.270
By hitting the heart with a pinpoint corkscrew blow,

00:18:20.140 --> 00:18:23.820
he's able to completely paralyze his opponent for an instant.

00:18:24.460 --> 00:18:27.700
A genuine magic punch!

00:18:28.760 --> 00:18:30.410
Date-san still has that!

00:18:30.640 --> 00:18:34.410
Yeah, it's a big shot that would normally never hit Ricardo,

00:18:34.410 --> 00:18:38.920
but now that he's not anticipating it and with the exhaustion from the first half setting in...

00:18:39.260 --> 00:18:40.130
Right!

00:18:40.130 --> 00:18:43.420
I bet Date-san is counting on that as well!

00:18:44.210 --> 00:18:46.400
That's why he withstood all this!

00:18:46.400 --> 00:18:48.680
He's been waiting for his chance!

00:18:48.960 --> 00:18:53.110
For the chance to use his magic punch, the Heartbreak Shot!

00:18:53.810 --> 00:18:57.060
And there's the bell signaling the beginning of the ninth round.

00:18:57.750 --> 00:18:59.750
The champion takes the initiative again!

00:18:59.750 --> 00:19:02.070
The challenger is getting hammered and can only take the defensive!

00:19:02.410 --> 00:19:04.450
He's getting slaughtered.

00:19:09.240 --> 00:19:12.150
S-So when's he gonna use it!?

00:19:12.150 --> 00:19:14.250
He can't hold on much longer!

00:19:14.570 --> 00:19:18.460
<i>Damn it, old man! If you lose before you can fire it, then it'll all be for nothing!</i>

00:19:20.950 --> 00:19:22.350
<i>It's no good!</i>

00:19:22.350 --> 00:19:26.100
<i>If he takes any more of this, he won't be able to use the Heartbreak Shot!</i>

00:19:27.200 --> 00:19:28.010
<i>Does he...</i>

00:19:28.840 --> 00:19:32.510
<i>not have the strength to fight back anymore!?</i>

00:19:37.910 --> 00:19:39.320
A right!

00:19:39.320 --> 00:19:42.020
An explosion from the cannon erupts!

00:19:51.830 --> 00:19:54.400
He twists his neck to kill the impact!

00:19:54.400 --> 00:19:56.410
The champion's off balance!

00:19:57.670 --> 00:19:59.920
This is the challenger's chance!

00:20:00.970 --> 00:20:04.380
Whoa, but it's a punch that barely taps against the guard!

00:20:06.050 --> 00:20:08.420
Does he not have the strength to fight back!?

00:20:08.810 --> 00:20:09.380
No!

00:20:09.900 --> 00:20:11.180
He was gauging the distance!

00:20:14.400 --> 00:20:15.610
<i>A twisting punch?</i>

00:20:15.610 --> 00:20:17.690
<i>The corkscrew blow?</i>

00:20:17.960 --> 00:20:20.310
The champion's guarding his head!

00:20:20.800 --> 00:20:22.310
His heart's wide open!

00:20:22.650 --> 00:20:24.320
The perfect scenario...

00:20:28.710 --> 00:20:31.090
Go!

00:20:31.090 --> 00:20:33.830
Heartbreak Shot!
